This study investigates the tensor join of two weighted hypergraphs, a construct analogous to the tensor sum of graphs. Analogous results from graph theory, including conditions for regular and edge-regularity, are generalized here. This operation facilitates the spectral analysis of the Laplacian, adjacency matrices, and Seidel matrices of hypergraphs, as it allows these spectra to be expressed in terms of the spectral attributes of the constituent components. Furthermore, a formula for the tensor join of two $\mathcal{L}$-connected hypergraphs is presented. These developments hold potential utility for modeling and analyzing complex systems.

